collatz-fixed-barrier-power-saving
Copyright 2026 Hiroyuki Nashida

This repository contains the Lean 4 formalization accompanying the preprint
"A power-saving bound, uniform in the endpoint, for Collatz orbits that stay above a fixed barrier"
by Hiroyuki Nashida (Zenodo, 2026, doi:10.5281/zenodo.22986670).
It is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; a copy of the license is in LICENSE.


Third-party material included in this repository
-------------------------------------------------

patches/shaik-v4.30.patch is a derivative work of

  FirstPassageLinearTransport, the Lean formalization accompanying I. A. Shaik,
  "Polylogarithmic Descent for Almost All Collatz Orbits in Natural Density",
  https://github.com/shaikidris/FirstPassageLinearTransport,
  commit 7239f88d05d8262d4778f3c46f4560905052872f, directory lean/FirstPassageLinearTransport.
  Copyright (c) 2026 Idris Ali Shaik.
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The files were modified by this project (2026-09-25). As stated in the header of the patch:
  (1) 19 of the 24 files used were ported from Lean v4.15.0 to Lean v4.30.0-rc2 / Mathlib v4.30.0-rc2.
      No theorem or definition statement is changed; only proofs and notation (`∑ x in s` -> `∑ x ∈ s`,
      Mathlib renamings, changed `field_simp` behaviour, imports -> `import Mathlib`).
  (2) The new file FirstPassageLinearTransport/FixedBarrier.lean was added. It contains the fixed-target form
      `fixedBarrier_failure_count` of the estimate behind Theorem 5.3 of Shaik's manuscript, assembled by this
      project from existing lemmas of the library; it is not a theorem of the manuscript or a declaration of
      Shaik's repository.
The copyright notices in the headers of the original files are retained in the patched files. The original files
are not included in this repository: fetch_shaik.py downloads them from the repository above, applies the patch,
and checks the SHA-256 hashes of the result.

No other file of this repository is derived from third-party code. The Lean files in CollatzND/ and CollatzProof/
use the formalizations of Mazur and Shaik only through `import` and references to their declarations.


